    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`FusedMoEConfig.is_lora_enabled` is `lora_config is not None`. With attention-only LoRA (`--lora-target-modules q_proj k_proj v_proj o_proj`) the experts are never LoRA-wrapped, but every MoE layer still switches to its LoRA-capable kernel. This PR applies the same `target_modules` check the LoRA manager uses.\n\n## Claims\n\n- BF16 MoE + attention-only LoRA no longer fails at startup with `LoRA context must be set`.\n- NVFP4 MoE + attention-only LoRA keeps the FlashInfer TRT-LLM experts instead of Marlin: +25% throughput on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4.\n- No change when `target_modules` is unset or names the MoE module.\n\n## Validation\n\nGB300, TP1, random rank-8 adapter on q/k/v/o, 256 requests × 256 tokens:\n\n| Model | main, no LoRA | main, attention LoRA | this PR, attention LoRA |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4 | TRT-LLM, 19190 tok/s | Marlin, 15691 tok/s | TRT-LLM, 19681 tok/s |\n| Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (BF16) | TRT-LLM, 15503 tok/s | startup fails | TRT-LLM, 15509 tok/s |\n\nAdapter requests still apply with this PR (4/8 greedy prompts differ from base). GSM8K (1319, 5-shot, NVFP4, base requests): no LoRA 59.89%; main with the attention-LoRA engine 64.75% (MoE on Marlin); this PR 59.89%, identical to no LoRA.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/model_executor/layers/test_fused_moe_lora_target.py   # 3 passed\n```\n\n## Details\n\n- `_is_moe_lora_target` returns `True` when `target_modules` is unset, and otherwise `is_in_target_modules(layer_name, target_modules)`, the check `LoRAModelManager._match_target_modules` uses. It is evaluated once at construction.\n- Limitation: the manager also consults `packed_modules_mapping`, which `FusedMoEFactory` cannot see. No in-tree model maps the MoE module as a packed parent.\n- No open PR addresses this (searched \"moe lora target_modules is_lora_enabled\", \"lora attention only moe kernel\").\n- AI assistance (Claude Code) was used; I reviewed every changed line and the results.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
